            <div xml:id="d859">

                <pb facs="0745" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856B.01/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Curaçao</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Huddleston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curaçao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-12T10:00:00-04:30">May 12, 1940—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to the Department’s telegram May 10, midnight [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">noon?</hi>] and to my telegram of May 10, 3 p.m.<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d859-f1"/> The British cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Despatch</hi> arrived at Willemstad at 5 p.m., May 11. A proclamation of
                    the Governor of Curaçao, states that as part of The Netherlands this territory
                    is also at war with the German Reich but that its international political status
                    will remain as before; that the Government established here has resolved to
                    continue to remain in and to take care of this part of the Netherlands territory
                    on land and at sea and any help from outside from whomever it may come will be
                    refused and considered as unwelcome.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddleston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
